## Notes
- The page is the normal 50,000-rectangle demo (no `?bench` query); the fps counter is visible
  ("3 fps" desktop, "12 fps" mobile in this run) and the canvas shows the document.
- Both viewports have no horizontal overflow (`documentElement.scrollWidth == innerWidth`).
- The committed capture helper launches Chrome for Testing with the SwiftShader software renderer
  (`--use-gl=angle --use-angle=swiftshader --enable-unsafe-swiftshader`) because the screenshot
  browser must not depend on GPU availability. These screenshots are **visual evidence only and not
  performance evidence**: the 3/12 fps labels are functional, and the real-GPU 60 fps baseline is
  P2-04 (`reviews/evidence/P2-04-perf-20261025T151952Z.json`, ANGLE Metal Apple M2, p50 1.80 /
  p95 2.00 ms unlocked frame production; display-locked control p95 16.80 ms).
- The server and Chrome were started by this task and stopped afterwards; no process is left running.
